  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What Injection Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Data That Becomes Code",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Attacker-supplied data crosses a boundary and gets interpreted as code or commands instead of inert data. That crossing is the whole bug class."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Root Cause"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Untrusted data mixed into a control string",
            "Query, markup, or shell command built by concatenation",
            "One flat string reaches the interpreter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='\"",
            "q = q + name + \"'\"   # name: data or syntax?",
            "cur.execute(q)       # engine cannot tell"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Confusion"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Interpreter sees one string, no authorship tags",
            "Developer intent and attacker input arrive fused",
            "Quotes decide meaning; attacker supplies quotes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Trust Boundaries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HTTP params, path segments, headers, cookies",
            "Uploaded file names and file contents",
            "Responses from upstream services and queues",
            "Anything read back out of your own database"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Interpreters In Range"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Interpreter",
            "Payload lands in"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SQL engine",
              "query text"
            ],
            [
              "Browser parser",
              "HTML / JS"
            ],
            [
              "OS shell",
              "/bin/sh, cmd.exe"
            ],
            [
              "LDAP, XPath",
              "filter string"
            ],
            [
              "NoSQL, templates",
              "operator, expression"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Impact Spectrum"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Data theft, then auth bypass",
            "Data tampering, silent record edits",
            "Remote code execution, full host compromise",
            "Lateral movement into the internal network"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Standing",
          "items": [
            "Top of OWASP Top 10 for a decade+",
            "A03:2021 folds XSS into Injection",
            "Same defect, three interpreters"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Whole Handbook In One Line",
          "text": "Fix is structural separation of code from data — never filtering 'bad characters'."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Vulnerable Shape",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "name = request.args[\"name\"]",
            "sql = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE\"",
            "sql += f\" name='{name}'\"  # input is syntax"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "execFile(\"ping\", [\"-c\",\"1\",host], cb)  // safe",
            "// exec(\"ping \" + host) spawns /bin/sh"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "SQL Injection Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Input lands inside the quotes",
            "Close the quote and you own the clause"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Auth Bypass Classic"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Input",
            "WHERE becomes",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bob",
              "name='bob'",
              "normal"
            ],
            [
              "' OR '1'='1",
              "name='' OR '1'='1'",
              "always true"
            ],
            [
              "' OR 1=1--",
              "name='' OR 1=1",
              "rest cut"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Comment Truncation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- input: admin'--",
            "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='admin'--'",
            "  AND pass='whatever'  -- never evaluated"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "-- in most engines, # in MySQL",
            "/* */ works inline too",
            "Password check simply disappears"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. UNION Extraction"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' UNION SELECT username,password",
            "  FROM users--  -- pulls a foreign table",
            "' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL--  -- probe count"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Column count must match exactly",
            "Types must be compatible; pad with NULL",
            "ORDER BY 1,2,3.. finds the count fast"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Stacked Queries"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "'; DROP TABLE users--   -- second statement",
            "'; UPDATE users SET role='admin'--"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Driver",
            "Multi-statement"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "MySQLi query",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "PHP PDO/MySQL",
              "often yes"
            ],
            [
              "SQL Server",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "Postgres simple",
              "yes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Blind Boolean",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "No data comes back, but the page differs on true vs false. Every request leaks one bit."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' AND 1=1--   -- page renders normally",
            "' AND 1=2--   -- page empty / 404",
            "' AND SUBSTR(pass,1,1)='a'--  -- bit by bit"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Blind & Advanced SQLi",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Time-Based"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Zero visible feedback: read data via latency",
            "Slow response = condition was true",
            "Noisy, but works on blind write-only paths"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Engine",
            "Delay call"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "MySQL",
              "SLEEP(5)"
            ],
            [
              "Postgres",
              "pg_sleep(5)"
            ],
            [
              "SQL Server",
              "WAITFOR DELAY"
            ],
            [
              "Oracle",
              "dbms_lock.sleep"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Error-Based"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Force a DB error, read the message",
            "Leaks column names, types, versions",
            "CAST/CONVERT errors echo the value itself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' AND 1=CAST((SELECT pass FROM users",
            "  LIMIT 1) AS int)--  -- value in the error"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Second-Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "payload stored safely",
              "read back later",
              "concatenated into query",
              "fires on other path"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Insert used a placeholder; the report page did not",
            "Your own DB is an untrusted source",
            "Grep every sink, not just entry points"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Reconnaissance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Probe"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Version",
              "version(), @@version"
            ],
            [
              "Tables",
              "information_schema.tables"
            ],
            [
              "Columns",
              "information_schema.columns"
            ],
            [
              "Current user",
              "current_user, user()"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Detection Order",
          "text": "Break the quote, read the error, then downgrade to boolean, then to time. Latency is the last resort."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Prepared Statement",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Query template carries placeholders (? or :name)",
            "Values travel to the DB separately from the text",
            "Two channels, never one string"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Why It Cannot Break"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "send template",
              "parse + compile plan",
              "bind values",
              "execute"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Parameterised Queries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Structure is fixed before a value arrives",
            "A bound value can never become new syntax",
            "' OR '1'='1 is searched for as literal text"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Placeholder Styles"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "Looks like",
            "Seen in"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Positional",
              "?",
              "JDBC, SQLite"
            ],
            [
              "Numbered",
              "$1",
              "Postgres"
            ],
            [
              "Named",
              "​:id",
              "SQLAlchemy"
            ],
            [
              "Named",
              "@id",
              "SQL Server"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Python"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cur.execute(",
            "  \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name=%s\",",
            "  (name,))   # tuple of values, never % or f"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Java"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "PreparedStatement ps = c.prepareStatement(",
            "  \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name=?\");",
            "ps.setString(1, name);  // bound as literal"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Values Only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Placeholders bind values, not identifiers",
            "Table and column names cannot be bound",
            "Keywords like ASC/DESC cannot be bound"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "COLS = {\"name\": \"name\", \"age\": \"age\"}",
            "col = COLS.get(choice, \"name\")  # allowlist",
            "q = f\"SELECT * FROM t ORDER BY {col}\""
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. ORMs And Procs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hibernate, SQLAlchemy, ActiveRecord: safe by default",
            "raw(), text(), interpolation reopen the hole",
            "Stored procs help only if they parameterise inside",
            "Dynamic SQL built inside a proc is still injectable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Least Privilege (Depth)",
          "items": [
            "App account owns no DDL, no DROP",
            "No read access to other schemas",
            "Separate account for migrations"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cross-Site Scripting",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What XSS Buys",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Attacker JavaScript runs in the victim's browser inside the trusted origin of the vulnerable site. Same-origin policy protects the attacker, not you."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Flavours"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Payload lives",
            "Delivery"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Reflected",
              "in the request",
              "crafted link"
            ],
            [
              "Stored",
              "server-side row",
              "every viewer"
            ],
            [
              "DOM-based",
              "client JS only",
              "no round-trip"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reflected: URL param echoed straight into the response",
            "Stored: comment, profile, message — biggest blast radius",
            "DOM: server never sees the payload after the #"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. DOM-Based Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "const t = location.hash.slice(1)  // source",
            "el.innerHTML = t                 // sink",
            "// #<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Dangerous Sinks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "innerHTML, outerHTML, document.write",
            "eval, setTimeout(string), new Function",
            "setAttribute('href', ...) with javascript: URIs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Sources In The DOM"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "location, location.hash, location.search",
            "document.referrer, window.name",
            "postMessage event.data",
            "stored server data rendered into JS"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Impact"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cookie theft via document.cookie",
            "Session riding: requests as the logged-in user",
            "Keylogging and credential phishing overlays",
            "CSRF token theft, then worm propagation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Mutation XSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser re-parses and normalises inserted HTML",
            "A sanitised-looking string becomes executable after insertion",
            "Why hand-written sanitisers keep losing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "HttpOnly Is Partial",
          "text": "It blunts cookie theft only. The script still defaces, keylogs, and acts as the user with their live session."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Output Encoding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Encode At The Landing Spot",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Encode untrusted data at output time",
            "Encoding is chosen by the context it lands in",
            "One value, many contexts, many encodings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. HTML Body Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Char",
            "Entity"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<",
              "&lt;"
            ],
            [
              ">",
              "&gt;"
            ],
            [
              "&",
              "&amp;"
            ],
            [
              "\"",
              "&quot;"
            ],
            [
              "'",
              "&#39;"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Attribute Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always quote the attribute, then entity-encode",
            "Unquoted attributes break on a bare space",
            "Space lets an attacker append onerror="
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. JavaScript Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "html",
          "lines": [
            "<div id=\"d\" data-user=\"{{ name|e }}\"></div>",
            "<script>",
            "const n = d.dataset.user  // read, not build",
            "</script>"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never build script source from strings",
            "Ship data as JSON in a data-* attribute",
            "JS string escaping only if you must inline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. URL And CSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "encodeURIComponent for each param value",
            "Validate the scheme: block javascript: and data:",
            "Encode inside style values; untrusted CSS exfiltrates data",
            "expression()-style abuse still haunts legacy engines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Prefer Safe Sinks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "el.textContent = userText  // never parsed",
            "const a = document.createElement(\"a\")",
            "a.setAttribute(\"href\", safeUrl)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Framework Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Framework",
            "The hole"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "React",
              "dangerouslySetInnerHTML"
            ],
            [
              "Vue",
              "v-html"
            ],
            [
              "Django/Jinja",
              "|safe"
            ],
            [
              "Angular",
              "bypassSecurityTrust"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Output Encoding (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. When HTML Is Required"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "const clean = DOMPurify.sanitize(dirty)",
            "el.innerHTML = clean  // vetted allowlist",
            "// never a hand-rolled regex blocklist"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "CSP As Depth",
          "items": [
            "Restrict script-src to known origins",
            "Block inline script; use nonces",
            "Buys mitigation, not a substitute"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Output, Not Input",
          "text": "The same row renders into HTML, an attribute, and a URL. Encode per context at render time, never once on the way in."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Reaching The Shell",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Untrusted input reaches an OS shell command, so the attacker runs arbitrary system commands as the app user."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "os.system(\"ping -c 1 \" + host)  # shell parses",
            "os.popen(\"convert \" + filename)",
            "# one string again, new interpreter"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Metacharacters"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Char",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              ";",
              "chain always"
            ],
            [
              "&&  ||",
              "chain on status"
            ],
            [
              "|",
              "pipe output"
            ],
            [
              "$(..)  `..`",
              "substitute"
            ],
            [
              "newline",
              "new command"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Payload"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "host = 8.8.8.8; cat /etc/passwd",
            "ping -c 1 8.8.8.8; cat /etc/passwd",
            "# second command runs as the app user"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Argument Injection"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No shell needed: leading - poses as a flag",
            "A filename like --output=/etc/cron.d/x",
            "Changes program behaviour, not just its input",
            "Terminate options with -- where supported"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Fix: No Shell"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "subprocess.run(",
            "  [\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", host],",
            "  shell=False)  # argv, nothing re-parsed"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Array APIs hand args straight to execve",
            "No shell means no metacharacters to escape",
            "shell=True with concatenation is the whole bug"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Command Injection",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. If A Shell Is Forced"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import shlex",
            "cmd = \"ls \" + shlex.quote(name)",
            "# quoting is last resort; blocklists leak"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Strict allowlist of permitted values first",
            "Then proper quoting, never manual escaping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Remove The Interpreter"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Instead of",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "curl",
              "HTTP client lib"
            ],
            [
              "cp, mv",
              "file APIs"
            ],
            [
              "tar",
              "archive lib"
            ],
            [
              "convert",
              "imaging lib"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Contain The Blast",
          "items": [
            "Run as an unprivileged user",
            "Sandbox or container per job",
            "Read-only mounts, no egress"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Three Distinct Controls",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Control",
            "Asks",
            "Acts at"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Validation",
              "acceptable?",
              "entry"
            ],
            [
              "Parameterisation",
              "code or data?",
              "DB call"
            ],
            [
              "Encoding",
              "safe here?",
              "output"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Validation Is Not The Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Defense in depth, never the primary defense",
            "Valid data can still be a valid attack",
            "O'Brien is a real name and a SQL breaker",
            "Rejecting it breaks users, not attackers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Allowlist Beats Blocklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Approach",
            "Rule",
            "Fails how"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Allowlist",
              "known-good set",
              "too strict"
            ],
            [
              "Blocklist",
              "known-bad list",
              "missed variant"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Constrain by pattern, type, range, and set",
            "Blocklists always miss an encoding or variant"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Canonicalise First"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Decode to one form, then validate",
            "%3C, double-encoding, %252F",
            "Unicode homoglyphs and overlong UTF-8",
            "Validate once, after normalisation, never before"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Primary Fix Per Interpreter"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Interpreter",
            "Primary fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SQL",
              "parameterise"
            ],
            [
              "OS shell",
              "array exec"
            ],
            [
              "Browser",
              "context encoding"
            ],
            [
              "Templates",
              "auto-escape on"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Validation vs Encoding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Right Layer Or Nothing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "SQL escaping does not make data HTML-safe",
            "HTML escaping does not make data shell-safe",
            "There is no universal sanitise() function"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Types Are Free Defense"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "uid = int(request.args[\"id\"])  # ValueError",
            "cur.execute(\"...WHERE id=%s\", (uid,))",
            "# an int cannot carry syntax"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Layer Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "validate at entry",
              "parameterise / encode at boundary",
              "least privilege underneath"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Stripping Bad Characters",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "SeLeCt          # case flip",
            "SEL/**/ECT      # inline comment",
            "%2527           # double-encoded quote"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Case, comments, encoding, whitespace all bypass",
            "Stripping quotes changes data and still loses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Hand-Escaping Quotes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Numeric context needs no quotes at all",
            "Backslash edge cases undo the escape",
            "Charset tricks (GBK) rebuild the quote byte"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Sanitise Once, Reuse"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cleaned for HTML, later used in a URL",
            "Wrong context on output re-opens the flaw",
            "Storage should hold raw data, not pre-escaped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Trusting The Browser"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Client validation is UX, not a control",
            "curl sends raw requests with no JS at all",
            "Mobile clients and replayed requests skip it too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Remaining Hole"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = \"SELECT * FROM t ORDER BY \" + col",
            "cur.execute(q, ())  # values safe, name open",
            "# allowlist col before it reaches the string"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. \"The Args Are Internal\""
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "shell=True or exec(string) on trusted values",
            "Internal today, user-influenced next sprint",
            "Second-order path makes it reachable quietly"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. ORM Complacency"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Safe by default, unsafe on every raw escape hatch",
            "Grep for raw(), text(), execute(), interpolation",
            "One f-string in a repository undoes the layer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Turning Escaping Off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "dangerouslySetInnerHTML or |safe for convenience",
            "No sanitiser behind the bypass",
            "Every hatch needs DOMPurify or a review note"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. WAF As The Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bypassable by encoding and fragmentation",
            "A stopgap that buys time, not safety",
            "Never close the ticket on a WAF rule"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Loud Errors In Prod"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stack traces hand over schema and versions",
            "Log detail server-side, show a generic message",
            "Verbose errors turn blind SQLi into easy mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One Mental Model",
          "text": "Every injection is code/data confusion at an interpreter boundary. Keep the two separate and the class disappears."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. SQL",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always parameterise; never concatenate",
            "Allowlist identifiers and ORDER BY choices",
            "Least-privilege DB account, no DDL",
            "Audit ORM raw escape hatches"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. XSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Context-aware output encoding, every sink",
            "Prefer textContent over innerHTML",
            "Sanitise required HTML with DOMPurify",
            "CSP and HttpOnly as depth, not as the fix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Command"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Avoid the shell; pass args as an array",
            "Allowlist plus shlex.quote when forced",
            "Sandbox and least privilege underneath",
            "Native library beats shelling out"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Validation's Place"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Supporting layer, never the sole defense",
            "Allowlist, and canonicalise before checking"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Encode and parameterise at the boundary",
            "Per context, per sink, at output time",
            "Not once at input, not globally"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
