    "text": "' OR '1'='1 still works in 2026 — not because filters are weak, but because the query was a string. Nine chapters on how untrusted input turns into executed code across SQL, the browser, and the shell, plus the only two defenses that hold: parameterisation and context-aware output encoding. Swipe for the blind SQLi ladder, the encoding-by-context table, and the anti-pattern list worth grepping your repo for tonight.",
